<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">533 CE</h1><p class="ref-lede">533 CE in world history: 4 events and 2 deaths. 198 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/439">439 CE</a><a href="/years/451">451 CE</a><a href="/years/454">454 CE</a><a href="/years/476">476 CE</a><a href="/years/533" aria-current="page">533 CE</a><a href="/years/534">534 CE</a><a href="/years/552">552 CE</a><a href="/years/554">554 CE</a><a href="/years/618">618 CE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-2">2 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Mercurius becomes Pope John II, the first pope to change his name</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Roman priest Mercurius, reluctant to reign under the name of a pagan god, took the name John II on his consecration. Adopting a papal name later became the settled custom of the Church.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ad-decimum">Battle of Ad Decimum</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Ad Decimum was fought on 13 September 533 at the tenth milestone south of Carthage, where the Byzantine general Belisarius defeated the Vandal army of King Gelimer.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tricamarum">Battle of Tricamarum</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Tricamarum was fought in December 533 west of Carthage, where the Byzantine army of Belisarius defeated the Vandal king Gelimer and his brother Tzazon, who was killed.</p></div></li></ol></section>
